It is almost twelve o'clock at night, but the sky is still light.
It has a soft, blue color.
I am walking on the street with Eva and Peter.
We do not talk much.
Only our footsteps sound in the night.
I look at my friends.
Eva is smiling, and Peter looks tired but happy.
When I came here, I knew no one.
But a lot has changed since.
I have gotten a good everyday life, and I have met many people.
I have actually found real friends.
Peter was the first colleague that I talked to.
And Eva invited me to her home recently.
Now we are walking here together under the bright summer sky.
I have just turned thirty-two years old.
I have built a life that I love.
I finally feel completely at home in my new city.
